			<div class="content" id="post-content-1933152">
									

<blockquote>
<p>1) How does the Foundation have any idea of what its goal are, given how random the actions of its members are?</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>2) What sort of &quot;broader contextual analysis&quot; could take a huge collection of weird, random behavior and say &quot;yep, that weird stuff is having an effect on this thing and that other thing&quot;?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The entry was written post-Protocol. As part of the Protocol, SCP-1659 must send subjects for research periodically to allow the Foundation to understand it better. They can't cut them up or experiment on them or whatever, but they can interview subjects, gain a wider understanding of what exactly is going on, and research the larger implications. At the beginning, of course, they didn't have the level of understanding they do now.</p>

							</div>

								
					
