</blockquote>
<p>This entire leading paragraph is a fair criticism. As I said upthread, I wrote this with a sense that the Foundation felt the Sword of Damocles over their heads with this anomaly. And, in their view, they are picking between two bad options (I guess I'm stuck on that theme lately). I did try to acknowledge in the article that there are arguments against that, but this skip isn't really &quot;innocuous&quot; as such. It has the potential to do really, really harmful things if it wants to, and we have no understanding of whether it ultimately wants to. But I get where you're coming from.</p>
